    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25010131>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "As a result, planaria have an incredibly messy genome (indeed, worms are mixoploid—different numbers of chromosomes in each cell). Despite this, they have the most reliable anatomy: every fragment of a planarian regenerates a perfect worm each time.".
